  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MURYA, ComDev</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ComDev-Hope Sahel consortium is initiating the project entitled &quot;MURYA&quot; with the objective of creating, facilitating and monitoring influence clubs (media, cultural groups, school leaders) on accountability and citizen participation in two regions, Maradi andTillab&#xe9;ri. This will be done through capacity building of influence leaders and through training activities (implementation of appropriate communication tools) within the influence clubs that will be created whose role will be to conduct and encourage social inclusion activities. This project will be implemented in the two main towns mentioned above. Overall, the change sought is the effective involvement of all actors in the search for appropriate solutions to the issues raised on social inclusion through citizen participation and accountability at the level of the identified regions. Thus:-In Maradi, change is expected in terms of increasing the level of involvement and accountability of the identified actors in relation to social inclusion issues;-In Tillab&#xe9;ri, change is expected in the increased level of citizen participation in security issues.A &quot;CIVIC TECH&quot; event will be held in the regions on citizen participation and accountability in Niger and a communication campaign for behavioural change through participatory theatre, radio theatre and the setting up of a mobile radio. Several training sessions on the use of digital technology and the production of media communication tools.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communication for Development Organization (ComDev) started its activities in 2012 with the advent of PDEV I (Peace through Development). It expanded further with PDEVII. At the end of these two phases, the actors who participated in the implementation of the PDEV project came together and created ComDev. Indeed, having played a very noticeable role in the awareness-raising activities of PDEVI and II, some actors realised the need to communicate more with our populations, who are plagued by several concerns. Throughout the country, young volunteer activists have decided to take up the challenge of creating a structure specialising in communication for development. This is how ComDev was born, thanks to the will of a group of young Nigeriens. Today ComDev specialises in communication for behavioural change with &quot;an innovative and participatory approach that puts the community at the centre of development. Its slogan is &quot;A vous la Voix pour des Voies&quot;.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communication pour le Developpement</narrative>
  </participating-org>
